-- Q3497: ERP and Accounting Information Systems [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Each receipt and issue is recorded in real time, maintaining a continuous balance","Inventory is counted and valued only once at the end of the fiscal year","Inventory quantities are estimated using published industry benchmark averages","Inventory records are updated only when a physical count is performed quarterly"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per ASC 330 and COBIT 2019 APO14, a perpetual inventory system records every receipt, issue, transfer, and adjustment in real time, maintaining continuously updated records of inventory quantities and costs. Physical counts verify but are not the primary record-keeping basis.
Wrong (B): Counting and valuing inventory only at year-end describes the periodic inventory method, not the perpetual method that updates records with each transaction.
Wrong (C): Estimating quantities from industry benchmarks is not an inventory accounting method. Both perpetual and periodic systems rely on actual transaction data or counts.
Wrong (D): Updating records only after quarterly physical counts is a variation of the periodic approach and does not reflect perpetual inventory''s real-time recording.$EXPL$
