-- Q3505: Data Management and Lifecycle [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Creating new data records from original source transaction documents","Permanently destroying data that has exceeded its mandated retention period","Moving inactive data to cost-effective long-term storage for regulatory retention","Processing raw transactional data into meaningful summary information"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per COBIT 2019 DSS06.06 and NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 1, data archival involves moving inactive data that must be retained for legal or regulatory reasons to cost-effective long-term storage. Archived data is typically read-only and infrequently accessed.
Wrong (A): Creating new data from source transactions describes data creation or capture, the first stage of the data lifecycle, not archival of inactive records.
Wrong (B): Permanently destroying data describes data destruction or disposal, which occurs after the retention period expires. Archival preserves records rather than eliminating them.
Wrong (D): Processing raw data into meaningful information describes data transformation or analysis, not the archival process of moving inactive records to long-term storage.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3505;

-- Q3509: Data Management and Lifecycle [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Processes individual transactions in real time within an OLTP system","Extracts source data, transforms it into a consistent format, then loads it","Distributes web content to end users through a global delivery network","Performs multidimensional analytical queries across historical datasets"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per COBIT 2019 DSS06, ETL is the standard data integration process for populating a data warehouse. Data is extracted from heterogeneous source systems, transformed to reconcile differing formats and classifications, and loaded into the target warehouse.
Wrong (A): Processing individual transactions in real time describes OLTP system functionality, not the batch-oriented ETL process used for data warehouse population.
Wrong (C): Distributing web content through a global network describes a content delivery network (CDN), which is unrelated to data warehouse integration processes.
Wrong (D): Performing multidimensional analysis describes OLAP querying, which occurs after the warehouse is populated. ETL handles the data loading step, not the analytical querying.$EXPL$
