-- Q3517: Data Management and Lifecycle [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The IT director has authority because IT controls all technical infrastructure access","The data owner has ultimate authority over access and classification decisions","Neither has authority because only the compliance department can decide under HIPAA","The contractors'' project manager has authority over their team''s access requirements"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per COBIT 2019 APO01.06 and NIST SP 800-18 Section 3.1, the data owner is accountable for determining data classification levels and authorizing who may access the data asset. The IT director, as data custodian, implements access controls but cannot override the owner''s authorization decisions.
